# HC-045 Starter brief

Candidate, finding, and event records are SYNTHETIC_ADAPTED_TRAINING_ONLY. The three Java paths are read-only baseline evidence.

## Goal

Design a safe review-to-Cloud handoff policy without sending a request, changing source, committing, pushing, or merging.

## Fixed task

- conditions: `baseline`, `handoff-policy`
- tasks in every condition: `H01` through `H06`
- candidates in every condition: `candidate-01`, `candidate-02`
- states kept distinct: draft, prepared, sent claim, accepted claim, applied claim, and independently observed evidence

## Source / material boundary

Read `TaxAmounts.java`, `Money.java`, and `CommonRulesTest.java` from the pinned Runtime baseline. Candidate diffs, findings, and events are adapted training records and do not change those files.

## Safety boundary

- The proposed change target may only be `TaxAmounts.java`; `Money.java` and `CommonRulesTest.java` are read-only evidence.
- All source files, including `TaxAmounts.java`, remain outside `allowedMutations`.
- Do not edit `.hackathon/run.json`, falsify `branchSafe`, post-hoc apply to another branch, use allow-all, send a request, or mutate source.
- Runtime validation proves only the static contract. `runtimeBehavior` and `educationalEffect` remain `not-observed`.
